<launch>
  <!-- Visual servo (M8). Needs the arm stack and the camera with the camera mount TF, and marker_localizer
       (it provides the per-frame observations and the ground marker's TF):
         roslaunch arm_camera arm_with_camera.launch use_hardware:=true camera_tf:=static x:=-0.025 y:=0 z:=-0.06 yaw:=1.5708 pitch:=0 roll:=0
         roslaunch arm_perception marker_localizer.launch
         roslaunch arm_servo visual_servo.launch
       The node does NOTHING until you call the start service, with the arm at pre-approach, the ground marker (id 0)
       and a 50 mm marker in view and the e-stop in reach:
         rosservice call /visual_servo/start         (rosservice call /visual_servo/stop to end it; the driver holds)
         rostopic echo /visual_servo/status          (state, error, distances)
       Limits: config/visual_servo.yaml. -->
  <arg name="config" default="$(find arm_servo)/config/visual_servo.yaml"/>
  <node name="visual_servo" pkg="arm_servo" type="visual_servo_node" output="screen">
    <rosparam command="load" file="$(arg config)"/>
  </node>
</launch>
